      "text": "LIVE TRAFFIC INSIDE THE CELL NUCLEUS The cell must express proper levels of the right genes at the right time to maintain its state and type. This specificity demands constant and coordinated actions by numerous factors that organize and transcribe the genome. In the highly crowded and dynamic nucleus, how do genome regulators find the right genes at the right time? LEARN MORE MEET OUR TEAM JOIN US NEWS 3/1/2023 – Nguyen Lab opens in Bonner Hall! 7/5/2023 – Nguyen Lab assemble! Gavin, Edwin, Anetzy, Taújay, Helen, Rachel, and Sinclair join. Contact vuqnguyen@ucsd.edu 1 858 534 9110 9500 Gilman Dr, MC 0322 La Jolla, CA 92093 Site link Research Tools Papers Members Follow Us Facebook-f Twitter Tumblr Instagram Tripadvisor Pinterest-p Youtube © 2023 Nguyen Lab UCSD. All Rights Reserved.",
